For a subprobability $\eta\ll\sigma$ on the sphere satisfying <a href="#lc:cell-eq3" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="lc:cell-eq3">[lc:cell-eq3]</a>, let $q=\eta(S^{d-1})>0$. For Gaussian $A$ write $g_{\eta,A}$ for the Lebesgue density of $Az$ under $\eta$. Such densities exist almost surely since $A$ has rank $n<d-1$ and they exist for $\sigma$. We may evaluate a version by the liminf of mass densities on shrinking cubes (say radii $1/l,\ l\to\infty$), which gives the Lebesgue density almost everywhere by differentiation. With this latter evaluation, for every fixed $u$ we have $$\label{lc:cell-eq5}
\mathbb E_A g_{\eta,A}(Au)^k
 \le \left[\exp(Cd) q^{1-n/\alpha}m_0^{n/\alpha}\right]^k.$$
